The '''''Raddus''''', formerly known as the '''''Dawn of Tranquility''''', was an [[MC85 Star Cruiser]] that served as the [[flagship]] of [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]]. It was used by the [[Resistance]] during its [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] against the [[First Order]]. It was one of the last [[Starship|ships]] built before the signing of the [[Military Disarmament Act]] by the [[Galactic Empire]] and [[New Republic]]. The vessel gained the moniker ''Raddus'' upon its entry into the service of the Resistance, when Admiral [[Gial Ackbar]] petitioned to rename it in honor of the famed [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]], who had died in service of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Alliance]] at the [[Battle of Scarif]] after defying the Rebel Alliance's political leaders and choosing to fight against seemingly insurmountable odds.

==Characteristics==
===Engines===
[[File:MC85StarCruiserRaddus-SaVAoR.png|thumb|250px|left|The sublight engines]]
The ''Raddus'' possessed eleven sublight ion modules for engines, which also included an [[ion injection manifold]] and [[turbo injector]]s. Its thrust allocation matrix improved the efficiency of the engines.<ref name="ICS" /> The engines were powerful enough to outpace a fleet of [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyers]] for several hours.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

===Complement and crew requirements===
<div style="float:right">[[File:Raddus_hangar_bay.png|thumb|right|250px|A hangar bay]]</div>
The vessel maintained a skeleton crew of 1,139, although it could via augmentation undergo complete automation. Due to its lack of a full crew complement, most of the auxiliary decks of the ''Raddus'' were abandoned and sealed off. Owing to it formerly being a Mon Calamari&ndash;built MC85 Star Cruiser, the vessel maintained multiple aquatic species waterways. [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia's]] quarters were located at the top of the ship just above the primary command [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]]. In addition, it contained crew accommodation levels, which were located around the same area as the shield operations center. The ship was equipped with two primary [[hangar]] bays as well as vehicle maintenance and repair bays.<ref name="ICS" /> The ship carried various [[RZ-2 A-wing interceptor|RZ-2 A-wings]], [[T-70 X-wing starfighter|T-70 X-wings]], and [[U-55 orbital loadlifter|U-55 loadlifters]].<ref name="Episode VIII" /> The ''Raddus'' had a dedicated hangar that could accommodate four full [[bomber]] [[squadron]]s.<ref name="Bomber Command" />

===Bridge===
[[File:Raddus_Emergency_Bridge.png|thumb|250px|left|The emergency bridge]]
The primary command bridge was located at the bow of the ship, and contained a large [[holotable]] that displayed the ship's status.<ref name="Episode VIII" /> In the event that the command bridge was left critically damaged, it had an emergency bridge located in the ventral area.<ref name="ICS" /> The command chair of the emergency bridge contained control systems that allowed its occupant to pilot the ship by themself if necessary.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

===Armaments and defenses===
The ''Raddus'' was equipped with 18 heavy [[turbolaser]]s, 18 heavy [[ion cannon]]s, 12 [[point-defense laser cannon]]s, and 6 [[proton torpedo launcher]]s.<ref name="ICS" /> It was also outfitted with experimental [[deflector shield]]s that could withstand immense damage when correctly angled for incoming fire.<ref name="TSWB">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> Likewise, its advanced deflector shield envelope could extend far beyond its hull.<ref name="TROS Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> The shields were proven powerful enough to withstand the [[First Order]]'s assault on the fleeing [[Resistance]] fleet significantly longer than those of other vessels in the fleet.<ref name="ICS" />

==History==
===Early service===
<div style="float:right">[[File:AdmiralRaddus-ToppsClassic2019RO.png|thumb|right|250px|The Resistance flagship was named in honor of Rebel Alliance hero Admiral Raddus.]]</div>
The ''Raddus'' was a part of the [[New Republic]]'s [[New Republic Home Fleet|Home Fleet]] under the name ''Dawn of Tranquility'', before being retired, part due to treaties limiting heavy warships and part due to a lack of navy personnel. After being acquired by the Resistance, it was remodeled to be less crew intensive, eliminating systems and [[computer]]ization deemed unnecessary. In large part because of these modifications, it was considered a valued resource within the Resistance's cause and was renamed ''Raddus'' in honor of the fallen [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] hero [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] at the request of Admiral [[Gial Ackbar]]. It was constructed at multiple shipyards with several different species contributing to the construction efforts.<ref name="ICS" />

===Fighting the First Order===
Following [[Black Squadron (Resistance)|Black Squadron's]] failed [[Mission to Cato Neimoidia (Resistance)|mission]] to retrieve the explorer [[Lor San Tekka]] from [[Cato Neimoidia]], they rendezvoused aboard the ''Raddus''. Commander [[Poe Dameron]] and [[BB-8]] worked on repairing ''[[Black One]]''. General Organa then ordered them to prepare to launch in an instant once they tracked San Tekka out of hyperspace. When Pava realized that the tracker had been disabled, they returned to brief Organa.<ref name="Poe 24">[[Poe Dameron 24|''Poe Dameron'' 24]]</ref>

[[File:Raddus_Ship_at_DQar.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Raddus'' leads the Resistance evacuation fleet.]]
Immediately after the [[Battle of Starkiller Base|destruction]] of [[Starkiller Base]], the ''Raddus'' participated in the [[Battle of D'Qar|evacuation]] of [[D'Qar]]. With the base below evacuated and abandoned, soon to be destroyed by the First Order as well,<ref name="Episode VIII" /> the ''Raddus'' became the mobile command center of the Resistance.<ref name="Galaxy1">[[Star Wars Galaxy (2019) 1|''Star Wars Galaxy'' (2019) 1]]</ref> While Dameron and a team of [[MG-100 StarFortress SF-17 heavy bomber|bombers]] engaged the retaliating First Order forces, the remaining Resistance personnel was transferred to the orbiting ship. The ''Raddus'' jumped to [[lightspeed]], but was [[Hyperspace tracker|tracked]] through [[hyperspace]] by [[Snoke]]'s [[flagship]], the ''[[Supremacy]]'', and [[Battle of Oetchi|attacked]].<ref name="Episode VIII" />

Deploying [[TIE/fo space superiority fighter|TIE fighters]], [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] in [[Kylo Ren's TIE silencer|his]] [[TIE/vn space superiority fighter|TIE Silencer]] attacked the cruiser, destroying its main hangar, then directed his attack towards the bridge. Sensing his mother's presence on the ship through [[the Force]], Kylo hesitated and at last decided to not to fire. His two wingmen, however, including [[Lieutenant]] [[Poldin LeHuse]], carried on with the attack. The bridge was torn apart and exposed to the [[vacuum]] of [[Realspace|space]], killing most of [[Resistance High Command]], including Admiral Ackbar,<ref name="Episode VIII" /> and the others aboard, including Commander [[Sesfan]] of the [[Engineering Corps]] and [[Lieutenant]] [[Guila Angira]].<ref name="Training of Rey and Battle of Crait">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Training of Rey and the Battle of Crait}}</ref> General Organa was the only one who survived, as she used the Force to get back to safety.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

===Destruction===
{{Quote|Fire on that cruiser!|[[Armitage Hux]], in a futile attempt to stop the ''Raddus''{{'s}} kamikaze attack|<ref name="Episode VIII" />}}
<div style="float:right">[[File:HoldoLightspeed.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The ''Raddus''{{'s}} final moments]]</div>
Upon arrival at [[Crait]], the ship was evacuated by thirty lifeboats, with [[Vice Admiral]] [[Amilyn Holdo]] deciding to stay behind and command the vessel from its secondary command bridge, in order to draw the First Order away from the fleeing vessels. When the ''Supremacy'' targeted the lifeboats, Holdo turned the ''Raddus'' around and [[Holdo maneuver|rammed]] the [[Mega-class Star Dreadnought|''Mega''-class Star Dreadnought]] at lightspeed, destroying itself and inflicting serious damage to the ''Supremacy'', along with destroying several of the escorting First Order [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyers]] in the process.<ref name="Episode VIII" /><ref name="Poe 31">[[Poe Dameron 31|''Poe Dameron'' 31]]</ref>

